* text=auto eol=lf

*.blade.php diff=html
*.css diff=css
*.html diff=html
*.md diff=markdown
*.php diff=php

/.github export-ignore
.styleci.yml export-ignore

# Belt and braces against a release built from the wrong branch.
#
# `cloud/` is the private hosting layer. It is not on this branch and .gitignore keeps it from being
# committed here, but bin/build-release.sh packages with `git archive`, which reads the tree it is
# given rather than the working directory - so a tarball built from a branch that does carry it would
# contain billing, the managed key service and the storage implementations.
#
# .dockerignore already excludes it from images and ci.yml skips that job on console. git archive had
# no equivalent, and this is it. The real protection is tagging from origin/main; this is what makes
# getting that wrong recoverable rather than public.
/cloud export-ignore
